College Student Handbook
Student Rules and Regulations
1. Attendance

Students must maintain a minimum attendance of 75% in every course to be eligible for semester examinations.

Students having attendance below 75% may not be permitted to appear for the examinations unless permitted under university regulations.

2. Examination Rules

Students must carry their College Identity Card and Hall Ticket during examinations.

Mobile phones, smart watches, calculators (unless approved), Bluetooth devices, and other electronic gadgets are strictly prohibited inside the examination hall.

Any malpractice will result in disciplinary action according to university regulations.

3. Library Rules

The library is open from 8:30 AM to 8:00 PM on working days.

Students may borrow four books at a time for 14 days.

Late returns will incur a fine of ₹5 per book per day.

Silence must be maintained inside the library.

4. Hostel Regulations

Hostel students must return before 9:00 PM.

Visitors are permitted only during approved visiting hours.

Ragging is strictly prohibited and punishable under institutional and government regulations.

Students must maintain cleanliness in hostel rooms.

5. Dress Code

Students must wear formal dress during working days.

College ID cards must be displayed visibly while on campus.

Shoes are mandatory inside laboratories.

6. Laboratory Rules

Food and beverages are not allowed inside laboratories.

Students must follow laboratory safety procedures.

Any damaged equipment should be reported immediately to the lab instructor.

7. Internet Usage Policy

College Wi-Fi is intended only for academic purposes.

Downloading pirated or illegal content is prohibited.

Misuse of the campus network may result in suspension of internet access.

8. Placement Cell

Students must maintain at least 7.0 CGPA to participate in most campus recruitment drives.

Students must attend all scheduled placement training sessions.

Professional dress is compulsory during interviews.

9. Sports Facilities

The sports complex is open from 6:00 AM to 8:00 PM.

Students must carry their ID cards while using sports facilities.

Sports equipment should be returned after use.

10. Grievance Cell

Students may submit grievances through the Student Affairs Office or the online grievance portal.

All complaints are handled confidentially.

The grievance committee aims to resolve issues within 15 working days.

